Workload Profile & Target Query Specifications
Query Scenario A: Real-Time Customer Account Ledger Extraction
Business Objective: Retrieve the complete, balance-reconciled transaction history for a specific customer over the trailing 30 days, sorted chronologically for mobile app display.
Relational Operations:
Join CUSTOMERS to ACCOUNTS on customer_id.
Join ACCOUNTS to TRANSACTIONS matching either source or destination identifiers.
Filter on customer_id and initiated_timestamp >= Current_Date - 30 Days.
Order results by initiated_timestamp DESC.
Query Scenario B: High-Value Settlement Risk and Anomaly Filter
Business Objective: Scan all transfers executed within the past 4 hours that exceed $10,000 USD equivalent where the account status is flagged as high-risk or the KYC status is incomplete.
Relational Operations:
Join TRANSACTIONS with TRANSFER_DETAILS on transaction_id.
Join with ACCOUNTS on source_account_id.
Join with CUSTOMERS on customer_id.
Filter on amount >= 10000.00, initiated_timestamp >= Current_Time - 4 Hours, and (risk_score > 0.70 OR kyc_status <> 'Verified').
Query Scenario C: End-of-Day Ledger Reconciliation Audit
Business Objective: Aggregate total debits, credits, and net turnover across every active currency within a 24-hour cycle to verify overall double-entry balance equality.
Relational Operations:
Filter TRANSACTIONS on execution_status = 'Settled' and date boundaries.
Group by currency_code and transaction_type.
Compute SUM(amount), COUNT(transaction_id).
